on\">\n   395→                        GitHub Copilot CLI now supports Bring Your Own Key (BYOK) and local model configurations, giving enterprises more control over their AI deployments.\n   396→                    </div>\n   397→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   398→                        <div class=\"meta-row\"><span class=\"update-type\">Feature</span> <span class=\"accent-link\">2026-04-07</span></div>\n   399→                    </div>\n   400→                </div>\n   401→\n   402→                <div class=\"item\">\n   403→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   404→                        <span class=\"product-name\">Aider</span> — Version 0.56.0\n   405→                    </div>\n   406→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   407→                        Introduces prompt caching for Sonnet via OpenRouter for improved performance, new /report command for session summaries, and --chat-language switch for multi-language support.\n   408→                    </div>\n   409→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   410→                        <div class=\"meta-row\"><span class=\"update-type\">Release</span> <span class=\"accent-link\">2026-04-05</span></div>\n   411→                    </div>\n   412→                </div>\n   413→\n   414→                <div class=\"item\">\n   415→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   416→                        <span class=\"product-name\">Continue</span> — Version 1.3.38-vscode\n   417→                    </div>\n   418→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   419→                        Config.yaml fixes, workspace directory filtering capabilities, and support for .continue/configs directory structure.\n   420→                    </div>\n   421→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   422→                        <div class=\"meta-row\"><span class=\"update-type\">Release</span> <span class=\"accent-link\">2026-04-04</span></div>\n   423→                    </div>\n   424→                </div>\n   425→\n   426→                <div class=\"item\">\n   427→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   428→                        <span class=\"product-name\">GitHub Copilot</span> — Copilot SDK Public Preview\n   429→                    </div>\n   430→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   431→                        GitHub Copilot SDK entered public preview, allowing developers to build custom integrations and extend Copilot capabilities.\n   432→                    </div>\n   433→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   434→                        <div class=\"meta-row\"><span class=\"update-type\">Announcement</span> <span class=\"accent-link\">2026-04-02</span></div>\n   435→                    </div>\n   436→                </div>\n   437→\n   438→                <div class=\"item\">\n   439→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   440→                        <span class=\"product-name\">Windsurf</span> — Version 1.9600.41: Adaptive Model Router\n   441→                    </div>\n   442→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   443→                        Adaptive model router for intelligent task routing to optimal models, plus GPT-5.4 mini integration and various model updates.\n   444→                    </div>\n   445→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   446→                        <div class=\"meta-row\"><span class=\"update-type\">Release</span> <span class=\"accent-link\">2026-04-07</span></div>\n   447→                    </div>\n   448→                </div>\n   449→\n   450→                <div class=\"item\">\n   451→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   452→                        <span class=\"product-name\">Windsurf</span> — Version 1.9600.40: GPT-5.4 Mini Integration\n   453→                    </div>\n   454→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   455→                        Added GPT-5.4 mini model support for faster, more efficient code completion and generation tasks.\n   456→                    </div>\n   457→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   458→                        <div class=\"meta-row\"><span class=\"update-type\">Release</span> <span class=\"accent-link\">2026-04-06</span></div>\n   459→                    </div>\n   460→                </div>\n   461→\n   462→                <div class=\"item\">\n   463→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   464→                        <span class=\"product-name\">Windsurf</span> — Version 1.9600.38: Adaptive Model\n   465→                    </div>\n   466→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   467→                        Introduced Adaptive Model feature that dynamically selects the most appropriate AI model based on task complexity and context.\n   468→                    </div>\n   469→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   470→                        <div class=\"meta-row\"><span class=\"update-type\">Feature</span> <span class=\"accent-link\">2026-04-06</span></div>\n   471→                    </div>\n   472→                </div>\n   473→\n   474→                <div class=\"item\">\n   475→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   476→                        <span class=\"product-name\">Cursor</span> — Unified Request-Based Pricing Model\n   477→                    </div>\n   478→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   479→                        Cursor simplified pricing to a unified request-based model, replacing previous complex tier structures.\n   480→                    </div>\n   481→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   482→                        <div class=\"meta-row\"><span class=\"update-type\">Announcement</span> <span class=\"accent-link\">2026-04-01</span></div>\n   483→                    </div>\n   484→                </div>\n   485→\n   486→                <div class=\"item\">\n   487→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   488→                        <span class=\"product-name\">Cursor</span> — Memories Feature: Context Persistence\n   489→                    </div>\n   490→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   491→                        Memories feature allows Cursor to remember important project context and user preferences across sessions for more personalized assistance.\n   492→                    </div>\n   493→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   494→                        <div class=\"meta-row\"><span class=\"update-type\">Feature</span> <span class=\"accent-link\">2026-04-01</span></div>\n   495→                    </div>\n   496→                </div>\n   497→\n   498→                <div class=\"item\">\n   499→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   500→                        <span class=\"product-name\">Cursor</span> — Jupyter Notebook Support\n   501→                    </div>\n   502→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   503→                        Added support for Jupyter Notebook files with enhanced editing and AI assistance capabilities for data science workflows.\n   504→                    </div>\n   505→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   506→                        <div class=\"meta-row\"><span class=\"update-type\">Feature</span> <span class=\"accent-link\">2026-04-01</span></div>\n   507→                    </div>\n   508→                </div>\n   509→\n   510→                <div class=\"item\">\n   511→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   512→                        <span class=\"product-name\">Cursor</span> — One-Click MCP Server Installation\n   513→                    </div>\n   514→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   515→                        Simplified installation process for MCP (Model Context Protocol) servers with a single click, reducing setup complexity for external tool integrations.\n   516→                    </div>\n   517→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   518→                        <div class=\"meta-row\"><span class=\"update-type\">Feature</span> <span class=\"accent-link\">2026-04-01</span></div>\n   519→                    </div>\n   520→                </div>\n   521→\n   522→                <div class=\"item\">\n   523→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   524→                        <span class=\"product-name\">Cursor</span> — BugBot: Automatic PR Review Agent\n   525→                    </div>\n   526→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   527→                        BugBot provides automated pull request review capabilities, identifying issues and suggesting fixes before merge.\n   528→                    </div>\n   529→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   530→                        <div class=\"meta-row\"><span class=\"update-type\">Feature</span> <span class=\"accent-link\">2026-04-01</span></div>\n   531→                    </div>\n   532→                </div>\n   533→\n   534→                <div class=\"item\">\n   535→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   536→                        <span class=\"product-name\">Cursor</span> — Background Agents in Slack Integration\n   537→                    </div>\n   538→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   539→                        Cursor now supports launching Background Agents directly from Slack by mentioning @Cursor, enabling AI-powered workflows within team communication channels.\n   540→                    </div>\n   541→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   542→                        <div class=\"meta-row\"><span class=\"update-type\">Feature</span> <span class=\"accent-link\">2026-04-01</span></div>\n   543→                    </div>\n   544→                    <div class=\"feedback-section\">\n   545→                        <div class=\"feedback-quote\">\"I wish they'd keep the old philosophy of letting the developer drive and the agent assist. I still want to _code_, not vibe my way through tickets.\"</div>\n   546→                        <div class=\"feedback-source\">\n   547→                            — Medium <span class=\"feedback-sentiment sentiment-negative\">Negative</span>\n   548→                        </div>\n   549→                    </div>\n   550→                </div>\n   551→            </section>\n   552→\n   553→            <!-- Technical Insights Section -->\n   554→            <section class=\"section\" id=\"insights\">\n   555→                <div class=\"section-header\">Technical Insights</div>\n   556→\n   557→                <div class=\"item\">\n   558→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   559→                        <span class=\"type-badge type-discussion\">Discussion</span>\n   560→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/2/lenny-podcast-highlights/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">Agentic Engineering Conversation Highlights</a>\n   561→                    </div>\n   562→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   563→                        Simon Willison on Lenny's Podcast covering agentic engineering, coding agents, and the state of AI in 2026.\n   564→                    </div>\n   565→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   566→                        <div class=\"meta-row\">Simon Willison / Lenny Rachitsky</div>\n   567→                        <div class=\"tags\">\n   568→                            <span class=\"tag\">agentic-engineering</span>\n   569→                            <span class=\"tag\">coding-agents</span>\n   570→                            <span class=\"tag\">automation</span>\n   571→                        </div>\n   572→                    </div>\n   573→                </div>\n   574→\n   575→                <div class=\"item\">\n   576→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   577→                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">Technical</span>\n   578→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/2/gemma-4/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">Gemma 4: Most Capable Open Models</a>\n   579→                    </div>\n   580→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   581→                        Google released four new vision-capable Apache 2.0 licensed reasoning LLMs (2B, 4B, 31B, plus 26B-A4B MoE). Native video, images, and audio processing.\n   582→                    </div>\n   583→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   584→                        <div class=\"meta-row\">Simon Willison | 2026-04-02</div>\n   585→                        <div class=\"tags\">\n   586→                            <span class=\"tag\">gemma-4</span>\n   587→                            <span class=\"tag\">open-models</span>\n   588→                            <span class=\"tag\">vision-llms</span>\n   589→                        </div>\n   590→                    </div>\n   591→                </div>\n   592→\n   593→                <div class=\"item\">\n   594→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   595→                        <span class=\"type-badge type-opinion\">Opinion</span>\n   596→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/3/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">AI-Generated Security Reports: From Slop to Real Research</a>\n   597→                    </div>\n   598→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   599→                        Linux kernel security list went from 2-3 reports/week to 5-10/day with most being correct. Different AI tools finding same bugs.\n   600→                    </div>\n   601→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   602→                        <div class=\"meta-row\">Greg Kroah-Hartman, Daniel Stenberg, Willy Tarreau | 2026-04-03</div>\n   603→                        <div class=\"tags\">\n   604→                            <span class=\"tag\">ai-security-research</span>\n   605→                            <span class=\"tag\">vulnerability-research</span>\n   606→                            <span class=\"tag\">linux-kernel</span>\n   607→                        </div>\n   608→                    </div>\n   609→                </div>\n   610→\n   611→                <div class=\"item\">\n   612→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   613→                        <span class=\"type-badge type-opinion\">Opinion</span>\n   614→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/3/vulnerability-research-cooked/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">Vulnerability Research Transformed by AI</a>\n   615→                    </div>\n   616→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   617→                        Thomas Ptacek: Within months, agents will find zero-days by pointing at source trees. LLMs uniquely suited for pattern-matching and constraint-solving.\n   618→                    </div>\n   619→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   620→                        <div class=\"meta-row\">Thomas Ptacek | 2026-04-03</div>\n   621→                        <div class=\"tags\">\n   622→                            <span class=\"tag\">ai-security-research</span>\n   623→                            <span class=\"tag\">vulnerability-research</span>\n   624→                            <span class=\"tag\">coding-agents</span>\n   625→                        </div>\n   626→                    </div>\n   627→                </div>\n   628→\n   629→                <div class=\"item\">\n   630→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   631→                        <span class=\"type-badge type-opinion\">Opinion</span>\n   632→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/4/github-growth/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">GitHub Activity Surging: 275M Commits/Week</a>\n   633→                    </div>\n   634→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   635→                        GitHub COO: 275M commits/week, on pace for 14B in 2026. GitHub Actions grew from 500M minutes/week (2023) to 2.1B minutes in one week.\n   636→                    </div>\n   637→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   638→                        <div class=\"meta-row\">Kyle Daigle (GitHub COO) | 2026-04-04</div>\n   639→                        <div class=\"tags\">\n   640→                            <span class=\"tag\">github</span>\n   641→                            <span class=\"tag\">github-actions</span>\n   642→                            <span class=\"tag\">platform-metrics</span>\n   643→                        </div>\n   644→                    </div>\n   645→                </div>\n   646→\n   647→                <div class=\"item\">\n   648→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   649→                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">Technical</span>\n   650→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/5/research-llm-apis/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">LLM Provider HTTP APIs Research</a>\n   651→                    </div>\n   652→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   653→                        Simon Willison researching new abstraction layer for LLM library. Scripts and outputs for Anthropic, OpenAI, Gemini, and Mistral raw JSON APIs.\n   654→                    </div>\n   655→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   656→                        <div class=\"meta-row\">Simon Willison | 2026-04-05</div>\n   657→                        <div class=\"tags\">\n   658→                            <span class=\"tag\">llm</span>\n   659→                            <span class=\"tag\">apis</span>\n   660→                            <span class=\"tag\">claude-code</span>\n   661→                        </div>\n   662→                    </div>\n   663→                </div>\n   664→\n   665→                <div class=\"item\">\n   666→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   667→                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">Technical</span>\n   668→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/5/scan-for-secrets/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">scan-for-secrets: Tool to Scan Files Before Sharing</a>\n   669→                    </div>\n   670→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   671→                        Python tool v0.1 to scan files for secrets before publishing. Built with Claude Code using README-driven-development. CLI and Python API.\n   672→                    </div>\n   673→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   674→                        <div class=\"meta-row\">Simon Willison | 2026-04-05</div>\n   675→                        <div class=\"tags\">\n   676→                            <span class=\"tag\">security</span>\n   677→                            <span class=\"tag\">agentic-engineering</span>\n   678→                            <span class=\"tag\">claude-code</span>\n   679→                        </div>\n   680→                    </div>\n   681→                </div>\n   682→\n   683→                <div class=\"item\">\n   684→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   685→                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">Technical</span>\n   686→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/5/syntaqlite-playground/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">Syntaqlite Playground: SQLite Validation in Browser</a>\n   687→                    </div>\n   688→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   689→                        Web-based playground for syntaqlite SQLite linting tool. UI for formatting, parsing AST, validating, tokenizing queries using WebAssembly/Pyodide.\n   690→                    </div>\n   691→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   692→                        <div class=\"meta-row\">Simon Willison / Lalit Maganti | 2026-04-05</div>\n   693→                        <div class=\"tags\">\n   694→                            <span class=\"tag\">sqlite</span>\n   695→                            <span class=\"tag\">sql</span>\n   696→                            <span class=\"tag\">tools</span>\n   697→                        </div>\n   698→                    </div>\n   699→                </div>\n   700→\n   701→                <div class=\"item\">\n   702→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   703→                        <span class=\"type-badge type-opinion\">Opinion</span>\n   704→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/5/eight-years-three-months/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">Eight Years Wanting, Three Months Building with AI</a>\n   705→                    </div>\n   706→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   707→                        Lalit Maganti built syntaqlite SQLite parser in 3 months with Claude Code after procrastinating 8 years. AI excels at concrete problems but struggles with design decisions.\n   708→                    </div>\n   709→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   710→                        <div class=\"meta-row\">Lalit Maganti | 2026-04-05</div>\n   711→                        <div class=\"tags\">\n   712→                            <span class=\"tag\">sqlite</span>\n   713→                            <span class=\"tag\">ai</span>\n   714→                            <span class=\"tag\">vibe-coding</span>\n   715→                            <span class=\"tag\">architecture</span>\n   716→                        </div>\n   717→                    </div>\n   718→                </div>\n   719→\n   720→                <div class=\"item\">\n   721→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   722→                        <span class=\"type-badge type-opinion\">Opinion</span>\n   723→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/5/chatgpt-healthcare/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">ChatGPT Healthcare Usage Insights from OpenAI</a>\n   724→                    </div>\n   725→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   726→                        ~2M weekly messages on health insurance, ~600K from people in 'hospital deserts' (30 min drive to nearest hospital). 7/10 messages outside clinic hours.\n   727→                    </div>\n   728→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   729→                        <div class=\"meta-row\">Chengpeng Mou (OpenAI) | 2026-04-05</div>\n   730→                        <div class=\"tags\">\n   731→                            <span class=\"tag\">openai</span>\n   732→                            <span class=\"tag\">chatgpt</span>\n   733→                            <span class=\"tag\">healthcare</span>\n   734→                            <span class=\"tag\">llms</span>\n   735→                        </div>\n   736→                    </div>\n   737→                </div>\n   738→\n   739→                <div class=\"item\">\n   740→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   741→                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">Technical</span>\n   742→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/6/datasette-ports/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">datasette-ports: Find Running Datasette Instances</a>\n   743→                    </div>\n   744→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   745→                        Tool to solve losing track of multiple Datasette instances. 'datasette ports' lists all running instances with URLs, versions, databases, and plugins.\n   746→                    </div>\n   747→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   748→                        <div class=\"meta-row\">Simon Willison | 2026-04-06</div>\n   749→                        <div class=\"tags\">\n   750→                            <span class=\"tag\">datasette</span>\n   751→                            <span class=\"tag\">developer-tools</span>\n   752→                            <span class=\"tag\">python</span>\n   753→                        </div>\n   754→                    </div>\n   755→                </div>\n   756→\n   757→                <div class=\"item\">\n   758→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   759→                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">Technical</span>\n   760→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/6/cleanup-claude-code-paste/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">Cleanup Claude Code Paste Tool</a>\n   761→                    </div>\n   762→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   763→                        Simon Willison created web tool to clean up prompts copied from Claude Code terminal. Removes '❯' prompt, fixes wrapped-line whitespace, copy-to-clipboard button.\n   764→                    </div>\n   765→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   766→                        <div class=\"meta-row\">Simon Willison | 2026-04-06</div>\n   767→                        <div class=\"tags\">\n   768→                            <span class=\"tag\">tools</span>\n   769→                            <span class=\"tag\">claude-code</span>\n   770→                        </div>\n   771→                    </div>\n   772→                </div>\n   773→            </section>\n   774→        </div>\n   775→    </main>\n   776→\n   777→    <footer>\n   778→        <p>Agentic Coding Research Report | Generated on April 13, 2026</p>\n   779→        <p>\n   780→            <a href=\"#\">Archive</a> ·\n   781→            <a href=\"#\">About</a> ·\n   782→            <a href=\"#\">RSS Feed</a> ·\n   783→            <a href=\"#\">GitHub</a>\n   784→        </p>\n   785→    </footer>\n   786→</body>\n   787→</html>\n   788→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"
