    "oldString": "            <!-- Technical Insights Section -->\n            <section class=\"section\" id=\"insights\">\n                <div class=\"section-header\">Technical Insights</div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"type-badge type-discussion\">Discussion</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/2/lenny-podcast-highlights/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">Agentic Engineering Conversation Highlights</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Simon Willison on Lenny's Podcast covering agentic engineering, coding agents, and the state of AI in 2026.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <div class=\"meta-row\">Simon Willison / Lenny Rachitsky</div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">agentic-engineering</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">coding-agents</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">automation</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">Technical</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/2/gemma-4/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">Gemma 4: Most Capable Open Models</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Google released four new vision-capable Apache 2.0 licensed reasoning LLMs (2B, 4B, 31B, plus 26B-A4B MoE). Native video, images, and audio processing.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <div class=\"meta-row\">Simon Willison | 2026-04-02</div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">gemma-4</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">open-models</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">vision-llms</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"type-badge type-opinion\">Opinion</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/3/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">AI-Generated Security Reports: From Slop to Real Research</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Linux kernel security list went from 2-3 reports/week to 5-10/day with most being correct. Different AI tools finding same bugs.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <div class=\"meta-row\">Greg Kroah-Hartman, Daniel Stenberg, Willy Tarreau | 2026-04-03</div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">ai-security-research</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">vulnerability-research</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">linux-kernel</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"type-badge type-opinion\">Opinion</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/3/vulnerability-research-cooked/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">Vulnerability Research Transformed by AI</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Thomas Ptacek: Within months, agents will find zero-days by pointing at source trees. LLMs uniquely suited for pattern-matching and constraint-solving.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <div class=\"meta-row\">Thomas Ptacek | 2026-04-03</div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">ai-security-research</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">vulnerability-research</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">coding-agents</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"type-badge type-opinion\">Opinion</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/4/github-growth/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">GitHub Activity Surging: 275M Commits/Week</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        GitHub COO: 275M commits/week, on pace for 14B in 2026. GitHub Actions grew from 500M minutes/week (2023) to 2.1B minutes in one week.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <div class=\"meta-row\">Kyle Daigle (GitHub COO) | 2026-04-04</div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">github</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">github-actions</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">platform-metrics</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">Technical</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/5/research-llm-apis/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">LLM Provider HTTP APIs Research</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Simon Willison researching new abstraction layer for LLM library. Scripts and outputs for Anthropic, OpenAI, Gemini, and Mistral raw JSON APIs.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <div class=\"meta-row\">Simon Willison | 2026-04-05</div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">llm</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">apis</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">claude-code</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">Technical</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/5/scan-for-secrets/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">scan-for-secrets: Tool to Scan Files Before Sharing</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Python tool v0.1 to scan files for secrets before publishing. Built with Claude Code using README-driven-development. CLI and Python API.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <div class=\"meta-row\">Simon Willison | 2026-04-05</div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">security</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">agentic-engineering</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">claude-code</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">Technical</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/5/syntaqlite-playground/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">Syntaqlite Playground: SQLite Validation in Browser</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Web-based playground for syntaqlite SQLite linting tool. UI for formatting, parsing AST, validating, tokenizing queries using WebAssembly/Pyodide.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <div class=\"meta-row\">Simon Willison / Lalit Maganti | 2026-04-05</div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">sqlite</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">sql</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">tools</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"type-badge type-opinion\">Opinion</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/5/eight-years-three-months/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">Eight Years Wanting, Three Months Building with AI</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Lalit Maganti built syntaqlite SQLite parser in 3 months with Claude Code after procrastinating 8 years. AI excels at concrete problems but struggles with design decisions.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <div class=\"meta-row\">Lalit Maganti | 2026-04-05</div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">sqlite</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">ai</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">vibe-coding</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">architecture</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"type-badge type-opinion\">Opinion</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/5/chatgpt-healthcare/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">ChatGPT Healthcare Usage Insights from OpenAI</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        ~2M weekly messages on health insurance, ~600K from people in 'hospital deserts' (30 min drive to nearest hospital). 7/10 messages outside clinic hours.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <div class=\"meta-row\">Chengpeng Mou (OpenAI) | 2026-04-05</div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">openai</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">chatgpt</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">healthcare</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">llms</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">Technical</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/6/datasette-ports/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">datasette-ports: Find Running Datasette Instances</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Tool to solve losing track of multiple Datasette instances. 'datasette ports' lists all running instances with URLs, versions, databases, and plugins.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <div class=\"meta-row\">Simon Willison | 2026-04-06</div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">datasette</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">developer-tools</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">python</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">Technical</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/6/cleanup-claude-code-paste/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">Cleanup Claude Code Paste Tool</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Simon Willison created web tool to clean up prompts copied from Claude Code terminal. Removes '❯' prompt, fixes wrapped-line whitespace, copy-to-clipboard button.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <div class=\"meta-row\">Simon Willison | 2026-04-06</div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">tools</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">claude-code</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n            </section>\n        </div>\n    </main>",
    "newString": "        <!-- Right Column: Technical Insights -->\n        <section class=\"column technical-insights\">\n            <div class=\"column-header\">Technical Insights</div>\n            <div class=\"column-content\">\n\n                <div class=\"insight-item\">\n                    <div class=\"insight-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/13/\">The peril of laziness lost: LLMs lack human optimization incentives</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-author\">Bryan Cantrill — Blog</div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-description\">\n                        Bryan Cantrill argues that LLMs inherently lack the virtue of laziness - work costs nothing to an LLM, they don't feel need to optimize for future time, and will happily dump more onto a layercake of garbage. Left unchecked, LLMs will make systems larger, not better.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-meta\">2026-04-13</div>\n                    <span class=\"insight-type opinion\">opinion</span>\n                    <div class=\"topics\">\n                        <span class=\"topic\">ai</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">llms</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">ai-assisted-programming</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"insight-item\">\n                    <div class=\"insight-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/13/\">Servo browser engine now embeddable as Rust crate</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-author\">Simon Willison — Blog</div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-description\">\n                        Simon Willison explored the new servo v0.1.0 crate, which packages the Servo browser engine as an embeddable library for Rust. Claude Code built a servo-shot CLI tool that successfully renders URLs to PNG.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-meta\">2026-04-13</div>\n                    <span class=\"insight-type technical\">technical</span>\n                    <div class=\"topics\">\n                        <span class=\"topic\">rust</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">servo</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">browser-engine</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"insight-item\">\n                    <div class=\"insight-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/13/\">Steve Yegge: Google's AI adoption mirrors John Deere, industry frozen for 18 months</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-author\">Steve Yegge — Blog</div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-description\">\n                        Steve Yegge provocatively analyzes that Google engineering has the same AI adoption footprint as John Deere tractor company: 20% agentic power users, 20% outright refusers, 60% still using Cursor or equivalent chat tools.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-meta\">2026-04-13</div>\n                    <span class=\"insight-type opinion\">opinion</span>\n                    <div class=\"topics\">\n                        <span class=\"topic\">google</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">steve-yegge</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">ai</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"insight-item\">\n                    <div class=\"insight-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/12/\">MLX VLM with Gemma 4 E2B for audio transcription on macOS</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-author\">Simon Willison — Blog</div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-description\">\n                        Simon Willison tested audio transcription using the 10.28 GB Gemma 4 E2B model with MLX and mlx-vlm on macOS. The uv run recipe transcribes a 14-second .wav file with impressive accuracy.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-meta\">2026-04-12</div>\n                    <span class=\"insight-type technical\">technical</span>\n                    <div class=\"topics\">\n                        <span class=\"topic\">mlx</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">gemma</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">speech-to-text</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"insight-item\">\n                    <div class=\"insight-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/11/\">SQLite 3.53.0: Major release with ALTER TABLE constraints and query formatting</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-author\">Simon Willison — Blog</div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-description\">\n                        SQLite 3.53.0 is a significant release following the withdrawal of 3.52.0, with accumulated user-facing and internal improvements. Key features include ALTER TABLE can now add and remove NOT NULL and CHECK constraints.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-meta\">2026-04-11</div>\n                    <span class=\"insight-type technical\">technical</span>\n                    <div class=\"topics\">\n                        <span class=\"topic\">sql</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">sqlite</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">developer-tools</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"insight-item\">\n                    <div class=\"insight-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/10/\">OpenAI's voice mode uses older, weaker model than expected</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-author\">Simon Willison / Andrej Karpathy — Blog</div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-description\">\n                        Simon Willison notes that it's non-obvious to many people that OpenAI's voice mode runs on a much older, weaker model (GPT-4o era with April 2024 knowledge cutoff).\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-meta\">2026-04-10</div>\n                    <span class=\"insight-type opinion\">opinion</span>\n                    <div class=\"topics\">\n                        <span class=\"topic\">openai</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">voice-mode</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">ai-capability-gap</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"insight-item\">\n                    <div class=\"insight-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/6/cleanup-claude-code-paste/\">Cleanup Claude Code Paste tool</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-author\">Simon Willison — Blog</div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-description\">\n                        Simon Willison created a niche web tool to clean up prompts copied from the Claude Code terminal app. The tool removes the '❯' prompt, fixes wrapped-line whitespace, and joins lines into clean text.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-meta\">2026-04-06</div>\n                    <span class=\"insight-type technical\">technical</span>\n                    <div class=\"topics\">\n                        <span class=\"topic\">tools</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">claude-code</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"insight-item\">\n                    <div class=\"insight-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/6/datasette-ports/\">datasette-ports: Find all running Datasette instances</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-author\">Simon Willison — Blog</div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-description\">\n                        Simon Willison released datasette-ports, a tool to solve the problem of losing track of multiple Datasette instances running across different terminals.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-meta\">2026-04-06</div>\n                    <span class=\"insight-type technical\">technical</span>\n                    <div class=\"topics\">\n                        <span class=\"topic\">datasette</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">developer-tools</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">python</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"insight-item\">\n                    <div class=\"insight-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/5/chatgpt-healthcare/\">ChatGPT healthcare usage insights from OpenAI</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-author\">Chengpeng Mou (OpenAI) — Blog</div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-description\">\n                        Chengpeng Mou, Head of Business Finance at OpenAI, shared anonymized U.S. ChatGPT data showing significant healthcare usage: ~2M weekly messages on health insurance.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-meta\">2026-04-05</div>\n                    <span class=\"insight-type opinion\">opinion</span>\n                    <div class=\"topics\">\n                        <span class=\"topic\">openai</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">chatgpt</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">ai-ethics</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"insight-item\">\n                    <div class=\"insight-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/5/eight-years-three-months/\">Eight years of wanting, three months of building with AI</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-author\">Lalit Maganti — Blog</div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-description\">\n                        Lalit Maganti's deep dive into building syntaqlite, a SQLite parser, formatter, and verifier. After procrastinating for 8 years due to 400+ grammar rules, Claude Code helped build the first prototype in 3 months.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-meta\">2026-04-05</div>\n                    <span class=\"insight-type opinion\">opinion</span>\n                    <div class=\"topics\">\n                        <span class=\"topic\">sqlite</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">ai</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">ai-assisted-programming</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"insight-item\">\n                    <div class=\"insight-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/5/syntaqlite-playground/\">Syntaqlite Playground: SQLite validation in browser</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-author\">Simon Willison / Lalit Maganti — Blog</div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-description\">\n                        Simon Willison created a web-based playground for syntaqlite, Lalit Maganti's SQLite linting and verification tool. The playground provides UI for formatting, parsing into AST, and validating.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-meta\">2026-04-05</div>\n                    <span class=\"insight-type technical\">technical</span>\n                    <div class=\"topics\">\n                        <span class=\"topic\">sqlite</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">sql</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">tools</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"insight-item\">\n                    <div class=\"insight-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/5/scan-for-secrets/\">scan-for-secrets: Tool to scan files before sharing</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-author\">Simon Willison — Blog</div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-description\">\n                        Simon Willison released scan-for-secrets 0.1, a Python tool to scan files for secrets before publishing. The tool scans for literal secrets and common encodings.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-meta\">2026-04-05</div>\n                    <span class=\"insight-type technical\">technical</span>\n                    <div class=\"topics\">\n                        <span class=\"topic\">security</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">agentic-engineering</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"insight-item\">\n                    <div class=\"insight-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/5/research-llm-apis/\">Research into LLM provider HTTP APIs for new abstraction layer</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-author\">Simon Willison — Blog</div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-description\">\n                        Simon Willison is working on a major change to his LLM Python library. To help design a new abstraction layer for features like server-side tool execution, he had Claude Code analyze client libraries.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-meta\">2026-04-05</div>\n                    <span class=\"insight-type technical\">technical</span>\n                    <div class=\"topics\">\n                        <span class=\"topic\">llm</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">apis</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">json</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"insight-item\">\n                    <div class=\"insight-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/4/github-growth/\">GitHub platform activity surging: 275 million commits per week</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-author\">Kyle Daigle (GitHub COO) — Blog</div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-description\">\n                        Kyle Daigle, GitHub COO, reports massive platform growth. There were 1 billion commits in 2025. Now it's 275 million commits per week, on pace for 14 billion in 2026.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-meta\">2026-04-04</div>\n                    <span class=\"insight-type opinion\">opinion</span>\n                    <div class=\"topics\">\n                        <span class=\"topic\">github</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">github-actions</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"insight-item\">\n                    <div class=\"insight-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/3/vulnerability-research-cooked/\">Vulnerability research transformed by AI coding agents</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-author\">Thomas Ptacek — Blog</div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-description\">\n                        Thomas Ptacek analyzes how coding agents are fundamentally changing vulnerability research and exploit development. He predicts that within months, agents will find zero-days by pointing at source trees.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-meta\">2026-04-03</div>\n                    <span class=\"insight-type opinion\">opinion</span>\n                    <div class=\"topics\">\n                        <span class=\"topic\">ai-security-research</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">vulnerability-research</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"insight-item\">\n                    <div class=\"insight-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/3/\">AI-generated security reports: From slop tsunami to real vulnerability research</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-author\">Greg Kroah-Hartman, Daniel Stenberg, Willy Tarreau — Blog</div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-description\">\n                        Linux kernel maintainer Greg Kroah-Hartman and other security experts report a dramatic shift in AI-generated security reports. What started as 'AI slop' has transformed into genuinely useful vulnerability research.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-meta\">2026-04-03</div>\n                    <span class=\"insight-type opinion\">opinion</span>\n                    <div class=\"topics\">\n                        <span class=\"topic\">ai-security-research</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">linux-kernel</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"insight-item\">\n                    <div class=\"insight-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/2/gemma-4/\">Gemma 4: Byte for byte, the most capable open models</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-author\">Simon Willison — Blog</div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-description\">\n                        Google released four new vision-capable Apache 2.0 licensed reasoning LLMs sized at 2B, 4B, 31B, plus a 26B-A4B Mixture-of-Experts. The models feature unprecedented intelligence-per-parameter.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-meta\">2026-04-02</div>\n                    <span class=\"insight-type technical\">technical</span>\n                    <div class=\"topics\">\n                        <span class=\"topic\">gemma-4</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">google</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">open-models</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"insight-item\">\n                    <div class=\"insight-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/2/lenny-podcast-highlights/\">Highlights from agentic engineering conversation on Lenny's Podcast</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-author\">Simon Willison / Lenny Rachitsky — Podcast</div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-description\">\n                        Simon Willison was a guest on Lenny Rachitsky's podcast episode titled 'An AI state of the union: We've passed the inflection point, dark factories are coming, and automation timelines.'\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-meta\">2026-04-02</div>\n                    <span class=\"insight-type discussion\">discussion</span>\n                    <div class=\"topics\">\n                        <span class=\"topic\">agentic-engineering</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">coding-agents</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n            </div>\n        </section>\n    </main>",
    "originalFile": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n    <title>Agentic Coding Research Report - 2026-04-13</title>\n    <style>\n        * {\n            margin: 0;\n            padding: 0;\n            box-sizing: border-box;\n        }\n\n        body {\n            font-family: Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;\n            font-size: 10pt;\n            background-color: #f6f6ef;\n            color: #000000;\n            line-height: 1.4;\n        }\n\n        .container {\n            max-width: 1400px;\n            margin: 0 auto;\n            padding: 10px;\n        }\n\n        header {\n            background-color: #ff6600;\n            padding: 5px 10px;\n            margin-bottom: 15px;\n        }\n\n        header h1 {\n            font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n            font-size: 14pt;\n            font-weight: bold;\n            color: #000000;\n        }\n\n        header .date {\n            font-size: 9pt;\n            color: #000000;\n            margin-top: 3px;\n        }\n\n        .three-column-layout {\n            display: grid;\n            grid-template-columns: 40% 35% 25%;\n            gap: 15px;\n            margin-bottom: 20px;\n        }\n\n        @media (max-width: 1024px) {\n            .three-column-layout {\n                grid-template-columns: 1fr;\n            }\n        }\n\n        .column {\n            background-color: #ffffff;\n            border: 1px solid #d4d4d4;\n            border-radius: 2px;\n        }\n\n        .column-header {\n            background-color: #ff6600;\n            padding: 5px 10px;\n            font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n            font-size: 11pt;\n            font-weight: bold;\n            color: #000000;\n        }\n\n        .column-content {\n            padding: 10px;\n        }\n\n        .empty-state {\n            color: #828282;\n            font-style: italic;\n            padding: 20px 10px;\n            text-align: center;\n        }\n\n        /* New Products Styles */\n        .product-item {\n            margin-bottom: 15px;\n            padding-bottom: 15px;\n            border-bottom: 1px solid #eeeeee;\n        }\n\n        .product-item:last-child {\n            border-bottom: none;\n            margin-bottom: 0;\n            padding-bottom: 0;\n        }\n\n        .product-name {\n            font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n            font-size: 10pt;\n            font-weight: bold;\n        }\n\n        .product-name a {\n            color: #000000;\n            text-decoration: none;\n        }\n\n        .product-name a:visited {\n            color: #828282;\n        }\n\n        .product-name a:hover {\n            text-decoration: underline;\n        }\n\n        .product-description {\n            margin: 5px 0;\n            color: #000000;\n        }\n\n        .product-meta {\n            font-size: 8pt;\n            color: #828282;\n            margin-top: 5px;\n        }\n\n        .product-category {\n            display: inline-block;\n            background-color: #f0f0f0;\n            padding: 2px 6px;\n            border-radius: 3px;\n            font-size: 8pt;\n            margin-top: 5px;\n        }\n\n        .community-quotes {\n            margin-top: 8px;\n            padding: 8px;\n            background-color: #fafafa;\n            border-left: 3px solid #ff6600;\n            font-size: 9pt;\n            font-style: italic;\n            color: #555;\n        }\n\n        .community-quotes .quote {\n            margin-bottom: 5px;\n        }\n\n        .community-quotes .quote:last-child {\n            margin-bottom: 0;\n        }\n\n        /* Whitelist Updates Styles */\n        .update-item {\n            margin-bottom: 15px;\n            padding-bottom: 15px;\n            border-bottom: 1px solid #eeeeee;\n        }\n\n        .update-item:last-child {\n            border-bottom: none;\n            margin-bottom: 0;\n            padding-bottom: 0;\n        }\n\n        .update-title {\n            font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n            font-size: 9pt;\n            font-weight: bold;\n            margin-bottom: 5px;\n        }\n\n        .update-title a {\n            color: #000000;\n            text-decoration: none;\n        }\n\n        .update-title a:visited {\n            color: #828282;\n        }\n\n        .update-title a:hover {\n            text-decoration: underline;\n        }\n\n        .update-product {\n            color: #828282;\n            font-size: 8pt;\n            margin-bottom: 5px;\n        }\n\n        .update-description {\n            margin: 5px 0;\n            color: #000000;\n            font-size: 9pt;\n        }\n\n        .update-meta {\n            font-size: 8pt;\n            color: #828282;\n            margin-top: 5px;\n        }\n\n        .update-type {\n            display: inline-block;\n            padding: 2px 6px;\n            border-radius: 3px;\n            font-size: 8pt;\n            margin-top: 5px;\n            background-color: #e8f4e8;\n            color: #2d5016;\n        }\n\n        .update-type.feature {\n            background-color: #fff4e6;\n            color: #9f6000;\n        }\n\n        .update-type.announcement {\n            background-color: #e6f3ff;\n            color: #004080;\n        }\n\n        .community-feedback {\n            margin-top: 8px;\n            padding: 8px;\n            background-color: #fafafa;\n            border-left: 3px solid #ff6600;\n            font-size: 8pt;\n        }\n\n        .feedback-positive {\n            border-left-color: #28a745;\n        }\n\n        .feedback-negative {\n            border-left-color: #dc3545;\n        }\n\n        .feedback-neutral {\n            border-left-color: #6c757d;\n        }\n\n        /* Technical Insights Styles */\n        .insight-item {\n            margin-bottom: 15px;\n            padding-bottom: 15px;\n            border-bottom: 1px solid #eeeeee;\n        }\n\n        .insight-item:last-child {\n            border-bottom: none;\n            margin-bottom: 0;\n            padding-bottom: 0;\n        }\n\n        .insight-title {\n            font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n            font-size: 9pt;\n            font-weight: bold;\n            margin-bottom: 5px;\n        }\n\n        .insight-title a {\n            color: #000000;\n            text-decoration: none;\n        }\n\n        .insight-title a:visited {\n            color: #828282;\n        }\n\n        .insight-title a:hover {\n            text-decoration: underline;\n        }\n\n        .insight-author {\n            color: #828282;\n            font-size: 8pt;\n            margin-bottom: 5px;\n        }\n\n        .insight-description {\n            margin: 5px 0;\n            color: #000000;\n            font-size: 9pt;\n            line-height: 1.5;\n        }\n\n        .insight-meta {\n            font-size: 8pt;\n            color: #828282;\n            margin-top: 5px;\n        }\n\n        .insight-type {\n            display: inline-block;\n            padding: 2px 6px;\n            border-radius: 3px;\n            font-size: 8pt;\n            margin-top: 5px;\n            background-color: #f0f0f0;\n            color: #555;\n        }\n\n        .insight-type.opinion {\n            background-color: #fff4e6;\n            color: #9f6000;\n        }\n\n        .insight-type.technical {\n            background-color: #e8f4e8;\n            color: #2d5016;\n        }\n\n        .insight-type.discussion {\n            background-color: #e6f3ff;\n            color: #004080;\n        }\n\n        .topics {\n            margin-top: 5px;\n            font-size: 8pt;\n        }\n\n        .topic {\n            display: inline-block;\n            background-color: #f0f0f0;\n            padding: 2px 5px;\n            margin-right: 3px;\n            margin-bottom: 3px;\n            border-radius: 2px;\n            color: #666;\n        }\n\n        footer {\n            background-color: #ff6600;\n            padding: 5px 10px;\n            font-size: 8pt;\n            color: #000000;\n            text-align: center;\n        }\n\n        footer a {\n            color: #000000;\n            text-decoration: underline;\n        }\n\n        footer a:hover {\n            text-decoration: none;\n        }\n\n        /* Print styles */\n        @media print {\n            body {\n                background-color: #ffffff;\n            }\n\n            .column {\n                border: 1px solid #000;\n                page-break-inside: avoid;\n            }\n\n            .column-header,\n            header,\n            footer {\n                background-color: #ddd !important;\n                -webkit-print-color-adjust: exact;\n                print-color-adjust: exact;\n            }\n\n            a {\n                text-decoration: underline;\n                color: #000;\n            }\n\n            .three-column-layout {\n                display: block;\n            }\n\n            .column {\n                margin-bottom: 20px;\n            }\n        }\n    </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n    <div class=\"container\">\n        <header>\n            <h1>Agentic Coding Research Report</h1>\n            <div class=\"date\">2026-04-13</div>\n        </header>\n\n    <main class=\"three-column-layout\">\n        <!-- Left Column: New Products -->\n        <section class=\"column new-products\">\n            <div class=\"column-header\">New Products</div>\n            <div class=\"column-content\">\n\n                <div class=\"product-item\">\n                    <div class=\"product-name\">\n                        <a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/sweep-ai\">Sweep AI</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"product-description\">\n                        AI coding assistant purpose-built for JetBrains IDEs (IntelliJ, PyCharm, Android Studio) that automates PRs and bug fixes with a task-based approach for precise goal expression.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"product-meta\">\n                        Released: 2025-04-07 | Source: Product Hunt\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"product-category\">IDE-integrated AI tool</div>\n                    <div class=\"community-quotes\">\n                        <div class=\"quote\">\"A marvelous first-step & and truly incredible first look at the future of programming\"</div>\n                        <div class=\"quote\">\"I've been using Sweep for a few months and its scary that with most tasks it gets everything right\"</div>\n                        <div class=\"quote\">\"I use this daily. It's 100x better than Github Copilot X and Code Interpreter\"</div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n            </div>\n        </section>\n\n        <!-- Middle Column: Whitelist Updates -->\n        <section class=\"column whitelist-updates\">\n            <div class=\"column-header\">Whitelist Updates</div>\n            <div class=\"column-content\">\n\n                <div class=\"update-item\">\n                    <div class=\"update-product\">Codex CLI</div>\n                    <div class=\"update-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/changelog\">Version 0.120.0: Realtime V2 Background Agent Streaming</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-description\">\n                        Codex CLI v0.120.0 (April 11, 2026) introduces Realtime V2 background agent streaming, custom TUI status lines, and code-mode tool declarations with MCP outputSchema support.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-meta\">2026-04-11</div>\n                    <span class=\"update-type release\">release</span>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"update-item\">\n                    <div class=\"update-product\">Gemini CLI</div>\n                    <div class=\"update-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://geminicli.com/docs/changelogs/\">Version 0.37.1: Latest Stable Release</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-description\">\n                        Gemini CLI v0.37.1 (April 9, 2026) is the latest stable release with performance improvements and enhanced multimodal capabilities.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-meta\">2026-04-09</div>\n                    <span class=\"update-type release\">release</span>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"update-item\">\n                    <div class=\"update-product\">GitHub Copilot</div>\n                    <div class=\"update-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog\">Copilot CLI Activity in Usage Metrics</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-description\">\n                        Copilot CLI usage is now included in organization usage metrics, providing better visibility into CLI-based AI assistant usage.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-meta\">2026-04-10</div>\n                    <span class=\"update-type feature\">feature</span>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"update-item\">\n                    <div class=\"update-product\">GitHub Copilot</div>\n                    <div class=\"update-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog\">Copilot Cloud Agent Validation Tools 20% Faster</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-description\">\n                        Validation tools in Copilot's cloud agent have been optimized to run 20% faster, improving response times for code review and validation tasks.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-meta\">2026-04-08</div>\n                    <span class=\"update-type feature\">feature</span>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"update-item\">\n                    <div class=\"update-product\">Windsurf</div>\n                    <div class=\"update-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://windsurf.com/changelog\">Version 1.9600.41: Adaptive Model Router</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-description\">\n                        Windsurf 1.9600.41 introduces adaptive model router for intelligent task routing to optimal models, plus GPT-5.4 mini integration and various model updates.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-meta\">2026-04-07</div>\n                    <span class=\"update-type release\">release</span>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"update-item\">\n                    <div class=\"update-product\">GitHub Copilot</div>\n                    <div class=\"update-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog\">Copilot CLI BYOK and Local Model Support</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-description\">\n                        GitHub Copilot CLI now supports Bring Your Own Key (BYOK) and local model configurations, giving enterprises more control over their AI deployments.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-meta\">2026-04-07</div>\n                    <span class=\"update-type feature\">feature</span>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"update-item\">\n                    <div class=\"update-product\">Windsurf</div>\n                    <div class=\"update-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://windsurf.com/changelog\">Version 1.9600.40: GPT-5.4 Mini Integration</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-description\">\n                        Added GPT-5.4 mini model support for faster, more efficient code completion and generation tasks.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-meta\">2026-04-06</div>\n                    <span class=\"update-type release\">release</span>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"update-item\">\n                    <div class=\"update-product\">Windsurf</div>\n                    <div class=\"update-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://windsurf.com/changelog\">Version 1.9600.38: Adaptive Model for Dynamic Selection</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-description\">\n                        Introduced Adaptive Model feature that dynamically selects the most appropriate AI model based on task complexity and context.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-meta\">2026-04-06</div>\n                    <span class=\"update-type feature\">feature</span>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"update-item\">\n                    <div class=\"update-product\">Aider</div>\n                    <div class=\"update-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://github.com/paul-gauthier/aider/releases\">Version 0.56.0: Prompt Caching and Report Command</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-description\">\n                        Aider v0.56.0 introduces prompt caching for Sonnet via OpenRouter for improved performance, new /report command for session summaries, and --chat-language switch for multi-language support.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-meta\">2026-04-05</div>\n                    <span class=\"update-type release\">release</span>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"update-item\">\n                    <div class=\"update-product\">Continue</div>\n                    <div class=\"update-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://github.com/continuedev/continue/releases\">Version 1.3.38-vscode: Config Fixes and Workspace Filtering</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-description\">\n                        Continue v1.3.38-vscode includes config.yaml fixes, workspace directory filtering capabilities, and support for .continue/configs directory structure.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-meta\">2026-04-04</div>\n                    <span class=\"update-type release\">release</span>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"update-item\">\n                    <div class=\"update-product\">GitHub Copilot</div>\n                    <div class=\"update-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog\">Copilot SDK Public Preview</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-description\">\n                        GitHub Copilot SDK entered public preview, allowing developers to build custom integrations and extend Copilot capabilities.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-meta\">2026-04-02</div>\n                    <span class=\"update-type announcement\">announcement</span>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"update-item\">\n                    <div class=\"update-product\">Cursor</div>\n                    <div class=\"update-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://cursor.sh/changelog\">Cursor 3: Background Agents in Slack Integration</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-description\">\n                        Cursor 3 now supports launching Background Agents directly from Slack by mentioning @Cursor, enabling AI-powered workflows within team communication channels. Also includes BugBot for automatic PR review, one-click MCP server installation, Jupyter notebook support, Memories feature for context persistence, and unified request-based pricing.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-meta\">2026-04-01</div>\n                    <span class=\"update-type feature\">feature</span>\n                    <div class=\"community-feedback feedback-negative\">\n                        \"Thirty minutes after the Cursor 3 announcement hit Hacker News, the top comment wasn't about a feature. It was a plea. 'I wish they'd keep the old philosophy of letting the developer drive and the agent assist,' one user wrote. 'I still want to _code_, not vibe my way through tickets.'\"\n                        <br><small>— Medium</small>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"update-item\">\n                    <div class=\"update-product\">Claude Code</div>\n                    <div class=\"update-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/whats-new/2026-w14\">Week 14 Updates: Computer Use in CLI, Interactive Lessons</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-description\">\n                        Claude Code Week 14 (March 30 - April 3, 2026) introduces computer use capabilities to the CLI, allowing Claude to open native apps, click through UI, test its own changes, and fix issues from the terminal. Also includes interactive lessons (/powerup), flicker-free rendering, MCP result-size overrides (up to 500K characters), and plugin executables added to PATH.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-meta\">2026-03-30</div>\n                    <span class=\"update-type feature\">feature</span>\n                    <div class=\"community-feedback feedback-neutral\">\n                        \"The timing is hard to ignore: just ten days ago, Anthropic sent legal threats to OpenCode, forcing them to remove built-in Claude authentication because third-party tools were using Claude Code's internal APIs to access Opus at subscription rates instead of pay-per-token pricing.\"\n                        <br><small>— Blog</small>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"community-feedback feedback-negative\">\n                        \"accidentally shipping your source map to npm is the kind of mistake that sounds impossible until you remember that a lot of the codebase was probably written by the AI you are shipping\"\n                        <br><small>— Blog</small>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n            </div>\n        </section>\n\n            <!-- Technical Insights Section -->\n            <section class=\"section\" id=\"insights\">\n                <div class=\"section-header\">Technical Insights</div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"type-badge type-discussion\">Discussion</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/2/lenny-podcast-highlights/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">Agentic Engineering Conversation Highlights</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Simon Willison on Lenny's Podcast covering agentic engineering, coding agents, and the state of AI in 2026.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <div class=\"meta-row\">Simon Willison / Lenny Rachitsky</div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">agentic-engineering</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">coding-agents</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">automation</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">Technical</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/2/gemma-4/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">Gemma 4: Most Capable Open Models</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Google released four new vision-capable Apache 2.0 licensed reasoning LLMs (2B, 4B, 31B, plus 26B-A4B MoE). Native video, images, and audio processing.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <div class=\"meta-row\">Simon Willison | 2026-04-02</div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">gemma-4</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">open-models</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">vision-llms</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"type-badge type-opinion\">Opinion</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/3/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">AI-Generated Security Reports: From Slop to Real Research</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Linux kernel security list went from 2-3 reports/week to 5-10/day with most being correct. Different AI tools finding same bugs.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <div class=\"meta-row\">Greg Kroah-Hartman, Daniel Stenberg, Willy Tarreau | 2026-04-03</div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">ai-security-research</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">vulnerability-research</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">linux-kernel</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"type-badge type-opinion\">Opinion</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/3/vulnerability-research-cooked/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">Vulnerability Research Transformed by AI</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Thomas Ptacek: Within months, agents will find zero-days by pointing at source trees. LLMs uniquely suited for pattern-matching and constraint-solving.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <div class=\"meta-row\">Thomas Ptacek | 2026-04-03</div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">ai-security-research</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">vulnerability-research</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">coding-agents</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"type-badge type-opinion\">Opinion</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/4/github-growth/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">GitHub Activity Surging: 275M Commits/Week</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        GitHub COO: 275M commits/week, on pace for 14B in 2026. GitHub Actions grew from 500M minutes/week (2023) to 2.1B minutes in one week.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <div class=\"meta-row\">Kyle Daigle (GitHub COO) | 2026-04-04</div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">github</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">github-actions</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">platform-metrics</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">Technical</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/5/research-llm-apis/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">LLM Provider HTTP APIs Research</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Simon Willison researching new abstraction layer for LLM library. Scripts and outputs for Anthropic, OpenAI, Gemini, and Mistral raw JSON APIs.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <div class=\"meta-row\">Simon Willison | 2026-04-05</div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">llm</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">apis</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">claude-code</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">Technical</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/5/scan-for-secrets/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">scan-for-secrets: Tool to Scan Files Before Sharing</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Python tool v0.1 to scan files for secrets before publishing. Built with Claude Code using README-driven-development. CLI and Python API.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <div class=\"meta-row\">Simon Willison | 2026-04-05</div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">security</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">agentic-engineering</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">claude-code</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">Technical</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/5/syntaqlite-playground/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">Syntaqlite Playground: SQLite Validation in Browser</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Web-based playground for syntaqlite SQLite linting tool. UI for formatting, parsing AST, validating, tokenizing queries using WebAssembly/Pyodide.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <div class=\"meta-row\">Simon Willison / Lalit Maganti | 2026-04-05</div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">sqlite</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">sql</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">tools</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"type-badge type-opinion\">Opinion</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/5/eight-years-three-months/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">Eight Years Wanting, Three Months Building with AI</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Lalit Maganti built syntaqlite SQLite parser in 3 months with Claude Code after procrastinating 8 years. AI excels at concrete problems but struggles with design decisions.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <div class=\"meta-row\">Lalit Maganti | 2026-04-05</div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">sqlite</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">ai</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">vibe-coding</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">architecture</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"type-badge type-opinion\">Opinion</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/5/chatgpt-healthcare/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">ChatGPT Healthcare Usage Insights from OpenAI</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        ~2M weekly messages on health insurance, ~600K from people in 'hospital deserts' (30 min drive to nearest hospital). 7/10 messages outside clinic hours.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <div class=\"meta-row\">Chengpeng Mou (OpenAI) | 2026-04-05</div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">openai</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">chatgpt</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">healthcare</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">llms</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">Technical</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/6/datasette-ports/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">datasette-ports: Find Running Datasette Instances</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Tool to solve losing track of multiple Datasette instances. 'datasette ports' lists all running instances with URLs, versions, databases, and plugins.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <div class=\"meta-row\">Simon Willison | 2026-04-06</div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">datasette</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">developer-tools</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">python</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">Technical</span>\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/6/cleanup-claude-code-paste/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">Cleanup Claude Code Paste Tool</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Simon Willison created web tool to clean up prompts copied from Claude Code terminal. Removes '❯' prompt, fixes wrapped-line whitespace, copy-to-clipboard button.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <div class=\"meta-row\">Simon Willison | 2026-04-06</div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">tools</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">claude-code</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n            </section>\n        </div>\n    </main>\n\n    <footer>\n        <p>Agentic Coding Research Report | Generated on April 13, 2026</p>\n        <p>\n            <a href=\"#\">Archive</a> ·\n            <a href=\"#\">About</a> ·\n            <a href=\"#\">RSS Feed</a> ·\n            <a href=\"#\">GitHub</a>\n        </p>\n    </footer>\n</body>\n</html>\n",
